      "text": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef main():\n    X = np.load('vectors.npy')  # (8000, 1024) float32, read-only usage\n    N, D = X.shape\n\n    # Compute squared norms with double precision for numerical accuracy\n    norms = np.einsum('ij,ij->i', X, X, dtype=np.float64)\n\n    total = 0.0\n    B = 1000  # block size, chosen to balance memory and speed\n    nblocks = (N + B - 1) // B\n\n    for bi in range(nblocks):\n        i0, i1 = bi * B, min((bi + 1) * B, N)\n        Xi = X[i0:i1]\n        ni = norms[i0:i1]\n\n        # ---- diagonal block (bi == bj) ----\n        G = Xi @ Xi.T  # float32 matmul (fast BLAS)\n        D2 = ni[:, None] + ni[None, :] - 2.0 * G.astype(np.float64)\n        np.maximum(D2, 0.0, out=D2)  # guard tiny negative values from rounding\n        Dm = np.sqrt(D2)\n        # only strict upper triangle counted once, then doubled for symmetry\n        s = np.triu(Dm, k=1).sum()\n        total += 2.0 * s\n\n        # ---- off-diagonal blocks (bj > bi) ----\n        for bj in range(bi + 1, nblocks):\n            j0, j1 = bj * B, min((bj + 1) * B, N)\n            Xj = X[j0:j1]\n            nj = norms[j0:j1]\n\n            G2 = Xi @ Xj.T\n            D2b = ni[:, None] + nj[None, :] - 2.0 * G2.astype(np.float64)\n            np.maximum(D2b, 0.0, out=D2b)\n            Db = np.sqrt(D2b)\n            total += 2.0 * Db.sum()\n\n    print(f\"TOTAL:{total!r}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
